  "overview": {
    "title": "Stone against the Atlantic",
    "p1": "The ramparts of the Portuguese City still draw a hard line between the medina and the ocean. The Bastion of the Angel is the standout viewpoint — a sea-facing platform that appears in almost every El Jadida photo essay.",
    "p2": "Walk the accessible sections for wind, horizon and a sense of how Mazagan was fortified. Surfaces can be uneven; wear steady shoes and mind the drop toward the rocks.",
    "p3": "Sunset is popular. Pair the walls with the cistern earlier the same day for a complete Portuguese circuit."
  },
